<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization, Sachs wound bypass regeneration, and open vs closed leaf venation loops (Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands))",
        "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization, Sachs wound bypass regeneration, and open vs closed leaf venation loops faithfully reproduces Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 53.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-auxin-canalization-leaf-veins-audit) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py> ;
    schema:about "Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py; output: docs/media/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_comparison.png; organism: Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: b1e95723b4cbd5f2bb79b0150dbb4ab3fc046d7542c48fe2c7644bb6175993d9; artifact_sha256: 565e6e4b22ecd61b308b65e0a1f0a0a075b46efeafa91532a20aadad70ea48d5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json=55e0f743ada83918..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg=7f67774708f8e952..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations.bib=95f1b35cf42a8ae7..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/scout_manifest.json=94a1d6a85fe649c5...}" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity>,
